  "text": "**The model sees little immediate difference if France kept their original attackers.** Restoring Dembélé instead of Kolo Muani changes France’s estimated xG by -0.0047 over the next 15 minutes; restoring Giroud instead of Thuram changes it by 0.0. Both effects are flagged negligible. These are separate substitution tests—not a joint simulation of cancelling the double change. [[ev:sb:3869685:1378]] [[ev:sb:3869685:1379]]\n\nIn reality, France’s pass share rose from 30% in the pre-change window to 53.9% afterward, but they still produced 0 shots and 0.0 xG; Argentina’s xG fell from 0.339 to 0.05. That suggests improved control rather than an immediate attacking breakthrough. The observational model cannot establish that keeping Giroud and Dembélé on changes the eventual result. [[ev:sb:3869685:1178]] [[ev:sb:3869685:1916]]",
